 "narrative": "## The trajectory\nRevenue was $34.6B in FY2025 [1].\nRevenue CAGR was +26.0% over FY2016..FY2025 [2].\nNet income was $4.3B in FY2025 [3].\n\n## Growth quality\nRevenue growth in FY2025 was +34.3% [1] [4].\nNet income growth in FY2025 was +164.2% [3] [5].\nIn FY2025, net income growth of +164.2% [3] [5] was above revenue growth of +34.3% [1] [4].\n\n## Margins\nGross margin was 49.5% in FY2025 [6].\nOperating margin changed +3.3pp in FY2025 [7] [8].\nNet margin changed +6.2pp in FY2025 [9] [10].\n\n## Cash & balance sheet\nIn FY2025, free cash flow of $6.7B [11] was above net income of $4.3B [3].\nThe current ratio was 2.85\u00d7 in FY2025 [12], above 1.00\u00d7.\nCash & equivalents was $5.5B in FY2025 [13].\n\n## Red flags\nLong-term debt grew +63.6% from FY2016 to FY2025. Source operands: Long-term debt USD 1,435,000,000 in FY2016 [14]; Long-term debt USD 2,348,000,000 in FY2025 [15].\n\n## What to watch next\nWatch whether revenue growth in the next reporting update improves from +34.3% in FY2025 [1] [4].\nWatch how net income in the next reporting update compares with $4.3B in FY2025 [3].\nWatch how operating margin in the next reporting update compares with 10.7% in FY2025 [7].",
